Hey @Gercov 👋 ,
This is not possible in a single Prisma operation. Our docs have this note about createMany:
You cannot create or connect relations - you cannot nest create, createMany, connect, connectOrCreate inside a top-level createMany
You could create a Channel and many Posts in a single query, but you could not nest another createMany under the Posts.
// this is possible
let result = await prisma.channel.create({
 data: {
 name: 'my channel',
 posts: {
 createMany: {
 data: [{ title: 'a post' }, { title: 'another post' }]
 }
 }
 }
})
// this is not allowed
let result = await prisma.channel.create({
 data: {
 name: 'my channel',
 posts: {
 createMany: {
 data: [
 { 
 title: 'another post',
 views: {
 createMany: {...} // cannot nest createMany inside createMany
 }
 }
 ]
 }
 }
 }
})
You could use a raw SQL query using $executeRaw or create the PostViews in a separate query.
