As a temporary backend-only workaround, if the legacy key is still available, create the admin client with the legacy service-role JWT rather than the sb_secret_... key:
const supabase = createClient(
 Deno.env.get('SUPABASE_URL')!,
 Deno.env.get('SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY')!,
 { auth: { autoRefreshToken: false, persistSession: false } }
)
Keep that key only in Edge Function secrets; do not put it in browser code, return it to clients, or log it. This should let you verify whether the failure is specifically the new-key/Auth Admin compatibility path while the support ticket is investigated. If the legacy secret has been removed, I would not mint a custom JWT as a workaround; the safer next step is to ask Supabase to confirm support for generateLink and getUserById with sb_secret_... after ES256 migration and provide the project/library versions without sharing any secret value.

